#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# real_sign

#% text
# `real_sign(x)` gives -1, 0 or 1 for a real number `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Symbolic and complex arguments stay unevaluated; machine numbers give machine numbers.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
real_sign(-2)
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
real_sign(-2.0)
#% output
#= -1.0

#% cell
real_sign(pi - 3)
#% output
#= 1

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sign`, `real_abs`
